# Citation metadata for styxx — see https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub's "Cite this repository" prompt renders preferred-citation below (the position paper), not this entry.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use styxx in research, please cite both the software and the position paper that motivates it."
title: "styxx: verification for the agent era"
abstract: >-
  styxx is a verification layer for the agent era, built on one principle: an instrument
  that cannot refuse cannot be trusted. Its instruments are in three layers. VERIFY asks
  whether a claim matches its evidence (certify, the OATH implementation; protocol; seal;
  diffgate and its GitHub Action; corpus_audit). MEASURE asks what is actually true about
  these minds (islands, coupling, mind, meaning_diff, crossmind and the register
  instruments). SENSE asks whether an agent can be connected to the world without lying
  about what it feels (sense). The diff gate's own real-world measurement went against it:
  a blind panel upheld 23 of 100 accusations sampled from 71,016 external agent-authored
  pull requests, precision 0.23 against a preregistered 0.95 floor. Its path accusation is
  withheld, and its GitHub Action reports by default and blocks only when a user sets
  soft-fail to false.
authors:
  - family-names: Rodabaugh
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: Fathom Intelligence
type: software
license: MIT
version: "7.50.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fathom-lab/styxx"
url: "https://styxx-org.netlify.app"
keywords:
  - agent-verification
  - claim-verification
  - receipts
  - preregistration
  - replication
  - representational-geometry
  - llm-observability
  - ai-safety

# Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest software release
